From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:59:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x: Add the ambient light sensor on
 the A7 iPads

Every A7 iPad has a CT819 light sensor at 0x39, which the tsl2583
driver serves as on the iPad 5 and 6.

The iPad mini 2 and 3 have it on i2c3 (Apple's device trees of J85-J87
and J85m-J87m: i2c3/als, interrupt GPIO 17), with an alsCalibration
that refers to the unit's SysCfg LSCI record; point als0 at it so that
the loader copies the record.

The iPad Air's trees (J71-J73) list it twice, on i2c0 and on i2c3
(als-i2c0 and als-i2c3, interrupt GPIO 6, both "probe-for-hardware"):
iOS probes for the one that is fitted. Describe both; the absent one
fails its chip ID read. Their alsCalibration is zero-filled with no
SysCfg reference, so the Air has no als0 alias and reports uncalibrated
lux.

i2c3 has nothing else described and is enabled for the sensor.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi  | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi | 23 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
index a908124..4a807b0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
@@ -331,6 +331,33 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The ambient light sensor: a CT819 at 0x39, on i2c0 or on i2c3. Apple's
+ * device trees of the J71, J72 and J73 carry both (i2c0/als-i2c0 and
+ * i2c3/als-i2c3, each with a proximity sensor beside it, interrupt
+ * GPIO 6) and iOS probes for the one fitted, so both are described: the
+ * absent one fails its chip ID read. Their alsCalibration is zero-filled,
+ * with no SysCfg reference, so the sensor reports uncalibrated lux and has
+ * no als0 alias for the loader.
+ */
+&i2c0 {
+	light-sensor@39 {
+		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
+		reg = <0x39>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 6 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c3 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	light-sensor@39 {
+		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
+		reg = <0x39>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 6 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+};
+
 /*
  * The battery gauge on UART5's HDQ line: a BQ27540 by Apple's device tree
  * (/arm-io/uart5/gas-gauge), the same on every A7 iPad. It runs the gauge
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
index de928e2..460683c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
@@ -369,6 +369,29 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The ambient light sensor, the same in the device trees of every iPad
+ * mini 2 and 3 (J85-J87, J85m-J87m: i2c3/als, als,ct819 at 0x39, interrupt
+ * GPIO 17). Its alsCalibration refers to the unit's SysCfg LSCI record,
+ * which the loader copies through the als0 alias.
+ */
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		als0 = &als;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c3 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/* m1n1 adds apple,als-calibration from the ADT */
+	als: light-sensor@39 {
+		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
+		reg = <0x39>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 17 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+};
+
 /*
  * The battery gauge on UART5's HDQ line: a BQ27540 by Apple's device tree
  * (/arm-io/uart5/gas-gauge), the same on every A7 iPad. It runs the gauge
